 ### SnowPakTool Desktop UI
 
-Under **Game data**, **Truck-Randomization** sits immediately after **Regions-Trucks**. It displays side-by-side Obtainable and Missions rule panes. The Obtainable pane records the six randomization rules (ownership, class, variety, progression, tires, and required addons); mission rules are not yet defined. This page documents the rules and does not apply randomization.
+Under **Game data**, **Truck-Randomization** sits immediately after **Regions-Trucks**. It displays side-by-side Obtainable and Missions rule panes. The Obtainable pane starts with the six randomization rules (ownership, class, variety, progression, tires, and required addons); Missions starts empty. Each pane has Add rule, and every rule has Edit and Remove actions. Edits save automatically between sessions; empty lists stay empty. This page documents the rules and does not apply randomization.
 
 A simple Windows Forms frontend is in `src/SnowPakTool.Desktop`. Its first tab handles PAK unpacking, workspace merging, and repacking. The **Experience / Ranks** tab displays and edits the `rankExp` progression values in `[ps]/rank_settings.sso`, shows the 17-season maximum of 1,163,997 XP, provides a collapsible region XP checklist with a selected subtotal, and totals the current rank progression values needed to reach level 30. The updated XP progression uses an exponential curve, with a steepness slider beside the curve preview and an XP reduction slider below it; the reduction amount appears beneath that slider.
 
